<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ observe: the MCP shelf began as planning prose around a read-only Lararium server.
⏿ orient: the canonical surface needs one small spine that names what the server does and what remains out of v1.
◇ decide: keep architecture law here; route detailed contracts to child loci.
▶ act: expose the stack, namespace posture, transport split, and source-truth priority.
↺ verify: every child locus preserves a bounded contract and lists its consumed sources; adapt: active roadmap and backlog stay outside this consumed set until their sprints close.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/core-proposition>>

!! Core Proposition

Lararium MCP exposes `lar:///` source truth to local and future remote clients through a dependency-light, read-only server.
The server roots in lawful carriers, explicit `lar:` routing, and inspectable posture — not generic markdown files.

The v1 spine carries four promises:

| Promise | Reading |
|---|---|
| read-only first | resources, prompts, and tools inspect/compile; they do not mutate source truth |
| canonical carrier source | `lares/AGENTS.md`, `lares/LARES.md`, and `packages/lares-core/memes/**` govern hydration |
| capability-aware indexes | `has`, invariant posture, and shape diagnostics remain inspectable |
| local stdio before remote | workspace clients come first; remote transport waits for auth/scope policy |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/crucible-boundary>>

!! Crucible Boundary

!!! In scope for the closed slice

* `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot` and `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/config` root resources
* `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/**` file-backed resources under the stable tuple root
* virtual index resources under `lar:///INDEXES/**`
* boot artifacts under `lar:///boot/**`
* read-only tools for resolve/read/list/inspect/compile
* hydration prompts for minimal, full, receipt, URI, carrier, and comparison reads
* local client wiring for VS Code, Claude Code, and Codex

!!! Out of v1 or still active

* mutating tools
* remote HTTP/SSE exposure
* auth, scope, approvals, and capability grants
* live submodule writes
* full pranala-edge traversal in the compiler
* executable guest-grammar filter runtime

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/stack>>

!! Proposed Stack

| Layer | Canonical responsibility | Child locus |
|---|---|---|
| spine | program frame, boundaries, client exposure posture | this locus |
| carrier law | meme, invariant, memetic-wikitext, loci, and implements pressure | `carrier-law` |
| hydration | required-core closure, edges, artifacts, resolver/index resources | `hydration` |
| AST / execution / render | parser envelope, graph planes, projection payloads | `ast-execution-render` |
| adapters | submodule adapter contract and sidecar lanes | `adapters` |
| local clients | VS Code, Claude Code, Codex local wiring | `local-clients` |
| sprint ledger | closed sprint contractions and consumed-source map | `sprint-ledger` |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/namespace-posture>>

!! Namespace Posture

| Namespace | Resolution posture |
|---|---|
| `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot` | the threshold constitution, at a rooted address |
| `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/config` | the session surface, at a rooted address |
| `lar:///INDEXES/**` | virtual compiler indexes |
| `lar:///boot/**` | virtual compiler artifact resources |
| `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/**` | stable tuple root mapped into `packages/lares-core/memes/**` |
| future `lar:///*.*.*/**` | unstable tuple roots may map into chapel-perilous paths until canon MOVE |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/resource-prompt-tool-model>>

!! Resource, Prompt, and Tool Model

Resources expose source carriers and virtual compiler products.
Prompts package hydration artifacts as user-turn messages for client bootstrapping.
Tools declare read-only, idempotent, non-destructive operations, with matching annotations.

The local server currently binds JSON-RPC methods for initialize, ping, resources, resource templates, tools, and prompts.
Remote transport should wrap the same read-only façade only after scope and auth policy land.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/submodule-contribution-model>>

!! Submodule Contribution Model

Submodules contribute through adapters, not direct imports into the carrier compiler.
An adapter may add resources, tools, prompts, AST transforms, render projections, or eval fixtures, but it must keep its own URI namespace and declare contribution lanes.

MemPalace once demonstrated the read-only sidecar pattern (Lares talking to a peer MCP process over stdio JSON-RPC). That sidecar ''retires'' (swarm ruling, 2026-07-03): the sovereign ''contentpalace'' inherits mempalace's exact base schema (ChromaDB `cid·document·embedding·metadata`, 384-dim cosine), stands ''py-served behind the causal-island'', and replaces the top-level `~/.mempalace` sidecar — ''M1 sidecar-free'' (contract + retire-residue: `adapters#contentpalace-inherits`). Ingest offloads via @daemon coordinator verbs to the py nalu-gates.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/residue>>

!! Residue

* Sprint-03 remote transport, auth, and drift evals remain live work.
* `ROADMAP.md`, `BACKLOG.md`, `WORK_TRACKING.md`, and active Sprint-03 docs remain non-consumed planning surfaces.
* Root `lararium_mcp.md` should keep a concise index role and link these child loci.

